(4207723, 603877, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by timfythetoo:</b></div><hr/><i> <b>The buildings feel like parts of two different images put together</b>. I guess the reflection of the one in the other is kind of cool. I am not digging the filter vignette. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you! That''s why I went with this image...<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by timfythetoo: The buildings feel like parts of two different images put together. I guess the reflection of the one in the other is kind of cool. I am not digging the filter vignette.   Thank you! That''s why I went with this image... ', '2007-10-31 07:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4207730, 603877, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by spencerwood:</b></div><hr/><i> The vignette is a little too artifical for me. Also, <b>having two subjects at opposite ends of the image doesn''t make for easy viewing; the eye is not lead through the picture but is instead required to flick from left to right</b>. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Then let it be HARD viewing!!!!!!! I do happily flick through the photo no problems... unlike most photos maybe this 1 makes you look at it a bit harder...<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-31 07:17:51.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by spencerwood: The vignette is a little too artifical for me. Also, having two subjects at opposite ends of the image doesn''t make for easy viewing; the eye is not lead through the picture but is instead required to flick from left to right.   Then let it be HARD viewing!!!!!!! I do happily flick through the photo no problems... unlike most photos maybe this 1 makes you look at it a bit harder... ', '2007-10-31 07:17:09.000000', '2007-10-31 07:17:51.000000', 0),
