(4220605, 602802, 84887, '<td valign="top">Post Challenge<br/> <br/>Wow, thanks for the votes and comments. Never expected to get a 4th with this one or now a ribbon by a unfortunate DQ. Especially after looking at some of the other entries in the challenge. <br/> <br/>This was not my original photo that I had planned on entering for this challenge. But a few days prior to the end of submission my wife had a client meeting at this building and suggested that I go down and take this photo, she thought it would make an interesting photo.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-04 16:07:14.</i></td>', 'Post Challenge Wow, thanks for the votes and comments. Never expected to get a 4th with this one or now a ribbon by a unfortunate DQ. Especially after looking at some of the other entries in the challenge.  This was not my original photo that I had planned on entering for this challenge. But a few days prior to the end of submission my wife had a client meeting at this building and suggested that I go down and take this photo, she thought it would make an interesting photo.', '2007-11-04 16:06:35.000000', '2007-11-04 16:07:14.000000', 0),
(4220614, 602609, 80904, '<td valign="top"><br/>At first I was puzzled on why this was disqualified, but then I realized that I made a bonehead mistake on this shot. Apparently I had hit the burn tool and streaked it without noticing. <br/>Here is the original that I had taken, I should have just submitted it instead.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//farm3.static.flickr.com/2344/1701788696_095dfebf83_o.jpg'', strrpos(''//farm3.static.flickr.com/2344/1701788696_095dfebf83_o.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//farm3.static.flickr.com/2344/1701788696_095dfebf83_o.jpg"/> <br/> <br/>Thanks again, until next ribbon.<br/>Jaime<br/></td>', 'At first I was puzzled on why this was disqualified, but then I realized that I made a bonehead mistake on this shot. Apparently I had hit the burn tool and streaked it without noticing. Here is the original that I had taken, I should have just submitted it instead.   Thanks again, until next ribbon.Jaime', '2007-11-04 16:15:15.000000', NULL, 0),
