(4330535, 602758, 60862, '<td valign="top">This strikes me as a test image to see how the lensbaby works, as opposed to a planned, competition-level image.  When we were doing the blur side challenge, a regular question was "why blur?"  Having such a small area in focus certainly drives my eye to the sharp part, but once there, I find nothing to hold my interest.  Now, if there had been someone in the window, or something falling to the ground, or a shaft of light, or a color, or something, that would''ve been different.<br/> <br/>When the "I Bought it on eBay" challenge ends tomorrow night, look at my image.  It has some similarities, but also some differenecs, so and see why you think the score is so much higher.  Like your shot, some commenters have said they don''t like the selective focus, but I have more who like where I drew their attention.</td>', 'This strikes me as a test image to see how the lensbaby works, as opposed to a planned, competition-level image.  When we were doing the blur side challenge, a regular question was "why blur?"  Having such a small area in focus certainly drives my eye to the sharp part, but once there, I find nothing to hold my interest.  Now, if there had been someone in the window, or something falling to the ground, or a shaft of light, or a color, or something, that would''ve been different. When the "I Bought it on eBay" challenge ends tomorrow night, look at my image.  It has some similarities, but also some differenecs, so and see why you think the score is so much higher.  Like your shot, some commenters have said they don''t like the selective focus, but I have more who like where I drew their attention.', '2007-12-22 22:03:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4351856, 604106, 82064, '<td valign="top">I was disappointed with this photo when I saw it on a "real" computer monitor. I only have a laptop (and a Panasonic Lumix and no tripod), so I didn''t realize how dark it was. I took this picture lying on my back trying to get a cool picture of the tree. The squirrel just happened to come along with his acorn. The white sky is common in Minnesota. <br/>I''m a beginner, but I''m learning!</td>', 'I was disappointed with this photo when I saw it on a "real" computer monitor. I only have a laptop (and a Panasonic Lumix and no tripod), so I didn''t realize how dark it was. I took this picture lying on my back trying to get a cool picture of the tree. The squirrel just happened to come along with his acorn. The white sky is common in Minnesota. I''m a beginner, but I''m learning!', '2008-01-01 22:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
